# Copy to `.env.local` (git-ignored) and fill in. Restart the dev server after.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL has a working fallback. The two Supabase variables below
# do not: without them the contact form still validates and still refuses to
# fake success, it shows the phone number instead, and the server logs why.

# ── Canonical origin (SEO) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The production domain, no trailing slash, e.g. https://www.example.com
#
# Feeds every canonical URL, the Open Graph metadataBase, every URL in
# sitemap.xml, the robots.txt sitemap pointer and every schema.org @id.
#
# LEAVE THIS UNSET LOCALLY AND ON PREVIEW DEPLOYS. It falls back to
# https://ryan-pressure-washing.vercel.app, which is what preview builds should
# be claiming — a preview that emits production canonicals tells Google the
# preview *is* the site.
#
# Set it in Vercel on the Production environment only. That is the single change
# needed when the real domain is registered.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# ── Lead storage (contact form → /api/leads → Supabase) ─────────────────────
#
# Project ref ikefommkvgktpjdtaxtf. The route writes to public.ryan_leads
# using the anon/publishable key — RLS on that table permits anon to INSERT
# only, so this key can add a row and nothing else, not read, edit or delete
# one. Names match what Vercel's Supabase integration provisions in
# production; the route only reads these two server-side, the NEXT_PUBLIC_
# prefix is just what the integration uses, not a sign this reaches the
# browser.
#
# No notification is sent anywhere yet — a submission becomes a row and
# nothing else. Someone has to look at the table (Supabase dashboard, or a
# query) to see it. Revisit once email/SMS delivery is wired back up.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://ikefommkvgktpjdtaxtf.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
